{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ldd54sfgyqu2rgbca32if2fudq5xrp6cjjwtztqks52kpgfd5bfq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The translation is complete and verified.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe C library is small — CMake globs a single translation unit:\n\n| File | Contents |\n|---|---|\n| `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` | builds `src/lib.c` into one SHARED lib |\n| `c_src/include/lib.h` | `tflac_u8`/`tflac_u32` typedefs, `struct tflac`, decl of `flac_validate` |\n| `c_src/src/lib.c` | `enum TFLAC_CHANNEL_MODE`, `tflac_size_memory`, `flac_validate` |\n\nI grepped for `#define` across `c_src/` — **no namespace/renaming macros**, so linker names equal source names.\n\n## Completion gate — symbol diff is empty\n\n```\n=== C exports (2) ===        === Rust exports (2) ===\nflac_validate                flac_validate\ntflac_size_memory            tflac_size_memory\n=== MISSING FROM RUST ===    (none)\n=== EXTRA IN RUST ===        (none)\n```\n\nNote `tflac_size_memory` is **not** declared in the public header but is non-`static`, so it is part of the exported ABI — it's translated and exported too.\n\n## Behavioral verification\n\nBuilt a `dlopen`-based differential harness comparing the C `.so` against the Rust `.so` over **1,190,575 calls**: edge/wrap-around sweeps of `tflac_size_memory` (including `0xFFFFFFFF`), the full cross product of interesting `blocksize`/`samplerate`/`channels`/`bitdepth` values, all `channel_mode`/`max_rice_value`/partition-order combinations, every `blocksize` in 16..=65535, and 300k randomized structs. Each line dumps the return value, all ten post-call fields, **and the raw 28 struct bytes** (so any layout/padding divergence would surface).\n\nResult: `cmp` clean, identical MD5 — and C at `-O0` matched C at `-O2`, confirming the reference is stable.\n\n## Fidelity details preserved\n\n- **Struct layout** confirmed against C via `offsetof`/`_Alignof`: size 28, align 4, offsets 0/4/8/12/16/17/18/19/20/24 (3 bytes tail padding before `cur_blocksize`).\n- **Exact check order** kept, including that `max_partition_order > 15` is rejected *before* the `min > max` comparison.\n- **Wrapping arithmetic** in `tflac_size_memory` via `wrapping_add`/`wrapping_mul`, matching C's `unsigned int` modulo-2³² semantics.\n- **No bug-fixing**: the `channel_mode` force-reset and the `else if (max_rice_value > 30)` branch (which is only reachable when `max_rice_value != 0`, so a nonzero-but-oversized value is rejected while zero is silently defaulted) are reproduced as-is.\n- The `while` loop's short-circuit order (modulo test first, then `partition_order < max_partition_order`) is preserved. I verified the shift amount can never exceed 16 given the preceding guards, so the divisor is never 0 — no Rust panic path exists where C had UB.\n\n`c_src/` was not modified; all scratch files went to `$TMPDIR` or `translation/target/` (630 MB of diff logs removed)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1106,"cache_read_input_tokens":31750,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1106,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"869d218d-96b3-45b7-9acd-d87340ca9cc2","uuid":"caeb21f5-3b47-4229-9e0a-3fe4b6db34ba","timestamp":"2026-08-26T21:04:22.948Z"}
